 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff_zeroHypercover", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff_zeroHypercover (\ud835\udcb0 : Precoverage.ZeroHypercover.{u} Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage X) : SmoothOfRelativeDimension n f \u2194 \u2200 i, SmoothOfRelativeDimension n (\ud835\udcb0.f i \u226b f)", "doc": "The criterion in `iff` form, for a consumer that wants to *use* the class on a cover.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/RelativeDimensionLocal.lean", "line": 102}
 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.JacobianData.smoothOfRelativeDimension_of_translation_cover", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem smoothOfRelativeDimension_of_translation_cover (d : JacobianData C) (n : \u2115) (\ud835\udcb0 : Precoverage.ZeroHypercover.{u} Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage d.J.left) (hcov : \u2200 i, SmoothOfRelativeDimension n (\ud835\udcb0.f i \u226b d.J.hom)) : SmoothOfRelativeDimension n d.J.hom", "doc": "**The S3 assembly, reduced to its two real inputs.** If the legs of a Zariski cover of `d.J.left` each have relative dimension `n` over the base, then so does `d.J.hom`.  The intended instantiation is worksheet \u00a73's chain: `Smooth d.J.hom` (S2) gives a standard-smooth chart at the identity, T5 pins its relative dimension to `genus C`, and the `k`-rational translations of X2 (`d.pointTranslationIso`) move that chart around \u2014 the legs of the cover being the translated charts, each of which has the identity's relative dimension by `smoothOfRelativeDimension_comp_iso`.  **What is a hypothesis here and why.** `\ud835\udcb0` is exactly the covering claim \u00a73.1 says remains owed: that the translated charts cover. It is not proved in this file, and a consumer must supply it. The value of the reduction is that the *pointwise* obligation \u2014 reach every scheme point, which `k`-rational translations may not do \u2014 is gone.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/RelativeDimensionLocal.lean", "line": 127}
 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.JacobianData.smoothOfRelativeDimension_pointTranslationIso", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem smoothOfRelativeDimension_pointTranslationIso (d : JacobianData C) (n : \u2115) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n d.J.hom] (x y : \ud835\udfd9_ (Over (Spec (.of k))) \u27f6 d.J) : SmoothOfRelativeDimension n ((d.pointTranslationIso x y).hom \u226b d.J.hom)", "doc": "**A translated chart inherits the relative dimension of the chart it came from.** The X2 transport, at the level the S3 criterion consumes: if `d.J.hom` has relative dimension `n`, so does its precomposition with any point translation.  Stated as the bridge between X2 (`AbelianVariety/Translation.lean`) and the covering criterion above, so that the S3 prover does not have to rediscover that `infer_instance` fails here.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/RelativeDimensionLocal.lean", "line": 139}
-{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.isMonHom_of_isProper_of_geometricallyIntegral", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem isMonHom_of_isProper_of_geometricallyIntegral {A B : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of K))} [MonObj A] [GrpObj B] [IsProper A.hom] [GeometricallyIntegral A.hom] [IsSeparated B.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType B.hom] (g : A \u27f6 B) (hg : \u03b7[A] \u226b g = \u03b7[B]) : IsMonHom g", "doc": "**A pointed morphism of group schemes is a homomorphism** (Milne, *Abelian Varieties*, I Cor 1.2; Mumford, *Abelian Varieties*, \u00a7II.4 p. 44, Corollary 1). Let `K` be an algebraically closed field, `A` a monoid object of `Over (Spec K)` whose underlying scheme is proper and geometrically integral over `K`, and `B` a group object whose underlying scheme is separated and locally of finite type over `K`. If `g : A \u27f6 B` is pointed (`\u03b7[A] \u226b g = \u03b7[B]`), then `g` is a homomorphism of monoid objects.  For `A` a group object this makes `g` a homomorphism of group objects: a monoid homomorphism automatically commutes with inversion (`CategoryTheory.inv_hom`).", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/RigidityCorollaries.lean", "line": 66}
+{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.isMonHom_of_isProper_of_geometricallyIntegral", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem isMonHom_of_isProper_of_geometricallyIntegral {A B : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of K))} [MonObj A] [GrpObj B] [IsProper A.hom] [GeometricallyIntegral A.hom] [IsSeparated B.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType B.hom] (g : A \u27f6 B) (hg : \u03b7[A] \u226b g = \u03b7[B]) : IsMonHom g", "doc": "**A pointed morphism of group schemes is a homomorphism** (Milne, *Abelian Varieties*, I Cor 1.2; Mumford, *Abelian Varieties*, \u00a7II.4 p. 44, Corollary 1). Let `K` be an algebraically closed field, `A` a monoid object of `Over (Spec K)` whose underlying scheme is proper and geometrically integral over `K`, and `B` a group object whose underlying scheme is separated and locally of finite type over `K`. If `g : A \u27f6 B` is pointed (`\u03b7[A] \u226b g = \u03b7[B]`), then `g` is a homomorphism of monoid objects.  For `A` a group object this makes `g` a homomorphism of group objects: a monoid homomorphism automatically commutes with inversion (`CategoryTheory.inv_hom`).       * Provenance: ADAPTED. * TO CHECK: the cited Mumford and Milne statements assume abelian-variety source and target, while this result weakens them to a proper geometrically integral monoid source and a separated locally finite-type group target; verify the hypothesis weakening.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/RigidityCorollaries.lean", "line": 78}
 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.JacobianData.smooth", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem smooth (d : JacobianData C) [GeometricallyReduced d.J.hom] : Smooth d.J.hom", "doc": "**S2: the Jacobian is smooth over `k`** (Kleiman \u00a75 `cor:sm`). A group scheme locally of finite type and geometrically reduced over a field is smooth (`smooth_of_grpObj`); the first two hypotheses come from the datum, and geometric reducedness is brick S1, taken here as an instance argument.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/JacobianSmooth.lean", "line": 74}
 {"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.JacobianData.smooth_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem smooth_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension (d : JacobianData C) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension (genus C) d.J.hom] : Smooth d.J.hom", "doc": "The frozen numeral degrades to bare smoothness: if the Jacobian is smooth of relative dimension `genus C` (brick S3) then it is smooth. Recorded here so consumers of the S3 instance need not rediscover `SmoothOfRelativeDimension.smooth`, and so that the two statements of the smoothness leg sit side by side.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/JacobianSmooth.lean", "line": 84}
-{"name": "CategoryTheory.CartesianMonoidalCategory.eq_comp_lift_id_of_comp_snd_eq", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem eq_comp_lift_id_of_comp_snd_eq {T X Y : C} {p : T \u27f6 X \u2297 Y} {y : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Y} (h : p \u226b snd X Y = toUnit T \u226b y) : p = (p \u226b fst X Y) \u226b lift (\ud835\udfd9 X) (toUnit X \u226b y)", "doc": "A morphism `p : T \u27f6 X \u2297 Y` whose second component is constant with value the point `y : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Y` factors through the slice `lift (\ud835\udfd9 X) (toUnit X \u226b y) : X \u27f6 X \u2297 Y` over `y`.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/Rigidity.lean", "line": 71}
-{"name": "CategoryTheory.CartesianMonoidalCategory.comp_eq_toUnit_comp_of_comp_snd_eq", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem comp_eq_toUnit_comp_of_comp_snd_eq {T X Y Z : C} {p : T \u27f6 X \u2297 Y} {y : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Y} {f : X \u2297 Y \u27f6 Z} {c : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Z} (h : p \u226b snd X Y = toUnit T \u226b y) (hf : lift (\ud835\udfd9 X) (toUnit X \u226b y) \u226b f = toUnit X \u226b c) : p \u226b f = toUnit T \u226b c", "doc": "If `f : X \u2297 Y \u27f6 Z` is constant on the slice over the point `y : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Y` (with value the point `c : \ud835\udfd9_ C \u27f6 Z`), then `f` composed with any morphism whose second component is constant with value `y` is constant with value `c`.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/Rigidity.lean", "line": 79}
-{"name": "AlgebraicGeometry.exists_eq_comp_of_isIso_appTop_of_range_subset", "kind": "theorem", "signature": "theorem exists_eq_comp_of_isIso_appTop_of_range_subset {V W : Scheme.{u}} {R : CommRingCat.{u}} (sV : V \u27f6 Spec R) [IsIso sV.appTop] (q : V \u27f6 W) {U : W.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hq : Set.range \u21d1q \u2286 (U : Set W)) : \u2203 z : Spec R \u27f6 W, q = sV \u226b z", "doc": "**Constancy of morphisms into affines.** A morphism `q : V \u27f6 W` of schemes, where all global sections of `V` come from a base ring `R` (`IsIso sV.appTop` for a structure morphism `sV : V \u27f6 Spec R`; e.g. `V` proper and geometrically integral over a field `R`) and the set-theoretic image of `q` is contained in an affine open `U` of `W`, is *constant*: it factors through the base as `q = sV \u226b z` for a point `z : Spec R \u27f6 W`.", "library": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild", "file": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/AbelianVariety/Rigidity.lean", "line": 97}
